# Deliberately accepted risks, each documented in detail (with technical
# justification, not just a version-cant-upgrade excuse) in the commit
# history and inline code comments. Each has an expiry date to force a
# periodic re-review, not a silent, permanent suppression.

# setuptools - fix requires >=83.0.0, which breaks Semgrep (pkg_resources
# ModuleNotFoundError, confirmed via actual rebuild+test, not assumed).
# CVE itself is macOS-only (APFS/HFS+ Unicode normalization bug in
# MANIFEST.in exclusion handling during sdist publishing) - this project
# runs Linux-only containers and never builds/publishes its own sdist.
# See commit ed13009.
CVE-2026-59890 exp:2027-02-28

# chromadb - verified via direct code review (vector_store.py) that the
# vulnerable code paths are never invoked: no embedding_function is ever
# passed to ChromaDB (all embeddings computed by our own provider
# abstraction), and ChromaDB is unreachable outside the internal Docker
# network with only the backend holding credentials. See commit 8f49231.
CVE-2026-45830 exp:2027-02-28
CVE-2026-45831 exp:2027-02-28
CVE-2026-45833 exp:2027-02-28

# protobuf - three separate fix attempts (exact 6.x pin, exact 5.x pin,
# ranged 5.x pin) all failed identically with pip resolution-too-deep.
# protobuf sits at the intersection of chromadb and semgrep (via
# opentelemetry) already-entangled dependency chains. Real fix tied to
# the chromadb upgrade above. See commit ccab4a4.
CVE-2025-4565 exp:2027-02-28

# msgpack GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 - confirmed FALSE POSITIVE, not deferred risk.
# msgpack is not installed anywhere in this image - verified twice via
# pip show inside the running container (Package(s) not found), the
# second time after a full --no-cache rebuild to rule out any local
# cache discrepancy with what CI built. Trivys own scan log shows why:
# WARN Third-party SBOM may lead to inaccurate vulnerability detection.
# This scan used an embedded/third-party SBOM rather than inspecting
# the image filesystem directly, and that SBOM is simply wrong here.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2027-02-28

# setuptools CVE-2025-47273 (Path Traversal in PackageIndex.download) -
# confirmed FALSE POSITIVE, not deferred risk. Fixed in 78.1.1; this
# project resolves to 80.10.2 (confirmed via pip show inside the
# running container), comfortably above the fix version and well
# within the separately-documented <81 cap. Same root cause as the
# msgpack false positive above: Trivys own log shows this scan used a
# third-party SBOM rather than the image filesystem directly.
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2027-02-28
